In Aptana it's very simple to set the <a href="http://svnbook.red-bean.com/en/1.4/svn.advanced.props.special.keywords.html">svn:keywords</a> property for a file.

For example if you want to set the svn keyword property <em><strong>Id</strong></em>:
<!--more-->
<ul>
    <li>In the file where you want to add the svn keyword property write <strong>$Id$</strong></li>
</ul>
<img title="Write the ID keyword in the file" src="{{ asset('uploads/article/' ~ article.id ~ '/id-file-300x235.gif') }}" alt="" width="300" height="235">
<ul>
    <li>Right click on the file, then follow Team -&gt; Set Property...<strong> </strong><strong>Note*</strong>: <em>Set Property...</em> will not be active if you haven't first added the file to SVN: <em>Team</em>-&gt;<em>Add to Version Controller</em></li>
</ul>
<img title="Select set property..." src="{{ asset('uploads/article/' ~ article.id ~ '/set-property-300x152.gif') }}" alt="" width="300" height="152">
<ul>
    <li>Select <strong>svn:keywords</strong>, and write <strong>Id</strong> in the text field <strong></strong></li>
</ul>
<img title="svn-keywords" src="{{ asset('uploads/article/' ~ article.id ~ '/svn-keywords-300x298.gif') }}" alt="" width="300" height="298">

When you make the SVN commit of the file, the <em>$Id$</em> keyword will be replaced with text in the format shown below:

<img title="Id keyword after commit" src="{{ asset('uploads/article/' ~ article.id ~ '/id-file-svn-300x141.gif') }}" alt="" width="300" height="141">

<h2 id="user-content-faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<div class="faq-list">
    <details class="acc" open>
        <summary>How do you set the svn:keywords property for a file in Aptana? <span class="chev">+</span></summary>
        <div class="acc-body">
            <p class="mb-0">Write the keyword marker (for example <strong>$Id$</strong>) in the file, then right click the file and follow Team -&gt; Set Property..., select <strong>svn:keywords</strong>, and write <strong>Id</strong> in the text field.</p>
        </div>
    </details>
    <details class="acc">
        <summary>Why is "Set Property..." not active when I right click the file? <span class="chev">+</span></summary>
        <div class="acc-body">
            <p class="mb-0">Set Property... will not be active if the file hasn't first been added to SVN. Use Team -&gt; Add to Version Controller before trying to set the property.</p>
        </div>
    </details>
    <details class="acc">
        <summary>What happens to the $Id$ keyword after an SVN commit? <span class="chev">+</span></summary>
        <div class="acc-body">
            <p class="mb-0">After the SVN commit of the file, the $Id$ keyword is replaced with text containing the file's SVN metadata, in a specific format.</p>
        </div>
    </details>
